# gate_type: implementation
# check-id	kind	arm	count	skip
# The implementation gate-3 rows: the manifest's `universal` row plus its `implementation` row, nothing else (g1 and g2 own the complement).
# Not wired into any runner; the generic gate program reads this file once it lands.
# kind `judgment` rows go to the one adjudicator seat (shard 1/1). Class per row = adjudication_by_gate[implementation], else adjudication.
# Rows for 17 (one arm per bug-fix-oneshot slug) is absent: it does not fit one argv row. 2c, 5 and 17 each run a second script today
# (suppression-lifetime; derive-stories --check; provenance): one row holds one arm.
# Checks 3, 7 and 19 stay judgment: their table proofs failed against the s322/s323 adjudicator verdicts.
# Checks 4, 8 and 10 stay judgment (map class llm) until the wiring flips them; validate-gate3-tables.sh ships unwired.
1	judgment	-	-
2	judgment	-	-
2a	script	validate-escalation-resolution.sh --escalations docs/escalations/pending.md --sprint {SPRINT} --transcript-dir {TRANSCRIPT_DIR}	legacy
2c	script	verdict.sh validate-escalation-status-vocabulary docs/escalations/pending.md	legacy
3	judgment	-	-
4	judgment	-	-
5	judgment	-	-
6	judgment	-	-
7	judgment	-	-
8	judgment	-	-
9	judgment	-	-
10	judgment	-	-
11	judgment	-	-
11a	judgment	-	-
12	lead	@close	-
13	lead	-	-
14	lead	@close	-
15	lead	@close	-
16	script	validate-stub-audit.sh --root {ROOT} --changed-from {BASE} {SHA}	legacy
19	judgment	-	-
22	judgment	-	-
25	script	validate-steering-budget.sh --count	legacy
26	script	@close	-
H1	lead	-	-
H2	script	validate-h2-attestation.sh --verify --sprint {SPRINT}	legacy
failure	lead	-	-
